  "facts": [
    "Opened on 14 March 2003, the Western Scheldt Tunnel became the Netherlands' longest highway tunnel at 6.6 kilometres, linking Ellewoutsdijk and Terneuzen beneath the Western Scheldt estuary.",
    "Each of the tunnel's two 11.3‑metre tubes houses two car lanes and features cross‑connections every 250 metres, automatically unlocking in emergencies to allow safe pedestrian passage.",
    "The tunnel's deepest point lies 60 metres below water level under the Pas van Terneuzen shipping lane, a feat achieved by a consortium including Franki Construct, Heijmans, and Royal BAM Group."
